<title>UK: RUGBY UNION-ENGLAND BEAT SCOTLAND 41-13.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-ENGLAND BEAT SCOTLAND 41-13.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>England beat Scotland 41-13 (halftime 16-10) in their Five Nations' championship match on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>England - Tries: Penalty try, Andy Gomarsall, Will Carling, Phil de Glanville. Conversions. Paul Grayson (3). Penalties: Grayson (5).</p>
<p>Scotland - Try: Ronnie Eriksson. Conversion: Rowen Shepherd. Penalties: Shepherd (2).</p>
